# The Dockerfile builds everything via `git clone` — the build context needs nothing
# but the Dockerfile itself. Exclude docs/CI so the context stays tiny.
#
# ONE EXCEPTION (vibe-ic#768): tools/pdk/ holds the PDK post-install patch the
# build applies to the prebuilt ciel volume. It cannot come from `git clone` —
# it patches THIS repo's own shipped artefact — and inlining it in a RUN heredoc
# would put the logic somewhere no test can import. Excluding everything under
# tools/ except that one directory keeps the context tiny.
*
!Dockerfile
!tools
tools/*
!tools/pdk
# SECOND EXCEPTION: the tool-manifest refresh. `/foss/pdks/versions.txt` is the
# BASE image's list and we replace several of the tools it names, so the compose
# rewrites it by PROBING the binaries. Both files must be in the context for the
# COPY to resolve -- and when they were not, the compose failed with
# `"/tools/tool_version_probes.tsv": not found` AFTER a 20-minute OpenROAD
# rebuild, because a build-context omission cannot be seen from anywhere except
# a build.
!tools/refresh_versions_manifest.sh
!tools/tool_version_probes.tsv
